# Skills maintenance

When you **add or materially change** product behavior, update agent memory in the **same task** (or PR) — do not leave skills stale.

## Agent workflow (every task)

1. **Before coding** — identify affected areas from the trigger table below; read the matching skill(s) and scoped rules.
2. **While coding** — follow documented pitfalls (middleware static matcher, Redis command budget, auth redirect allowlists, etc.).
3. **Before finishing** — complete the checklist below; do not mark work done with stale docs.

Skip doc updates only for typo fixes, pure refactors with **no** behavior change, or one-off scripts.

## Trigger table — what to read & update

| If you changed… | Read first | Update after |
|-----------------|------------|--------------|
| Auth pages, callback, middleware, navbar, password UX | `studyverce-auth` | skill + `nextjs-web.mdc` if middleware |
| Supabase email templates / `config.toml` auth email | `studyverce-auth` | skill `reference.md`, root `README.md` email section |
| `packages/redis`, `packages/rate-limit`, socket redis-cache, `/presence` | `studyverce-redis` | skill + root `README.md` budget table |
| Room UI, listing, socket events, presence | `studyverce-rooms` | skill + `room-features.mdc` |
| Post-its, tasks, todo panel | `studyverce-post-it-notes` | skill + `post-it-notes.mdc` |
| Dashboard shell / stats | `studyverce-dashboard` | skill |
| Schema, RLS, migrations | `supabase-migrations.mdc` + affected feature skill | migration + types + mapper |
| Cross-cutting layout, commands, new primary files | root `AGENTS.md`, `studyverce-overview.mdc` | index row in `.cursor/skills/README.md` |

## What to update

| Change area | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Any feature | Matching skill `SKILL.md` + `reference.md` if present |
| Room / listing / social | `studyverce-rooms` |
| Auth / session / email | `studyverce-auth` |
| Redis / rate limits / presence cache | `studyverce-redis` |
| Post-its / tasks | `studyverce-post-it-notes` |
| Dashboard | `studyverce-dashboard` |
| Cross-cutting layout or commands | `studyverce-overview.mdc`, root `AGENTS.md` |
| File-specific patterns | Relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| New feature domain | New skill under `.cursor/skills/<name>/` + row in `.cursor/skills/README.md` |

## Minimum doc updates per feature change

1. **SKILL.md** — workflow steps, pitfalls, and “where to look” for the new/changed behavior.
2. **reference.md** — tables (routes, components, actions, migrations, socket events, keys).
3. **AGENTS.md** — “Where to look” row if a new primary file or feature name.
4. **Rule `.mdc`** — short bullet if the change affects globs that rule covers.

## Skill frontmatter

Refresh the skill `description` in YAML when scope grows (so auto-routing still picks the right skill).

## Checklist before finishing (required)

- [ ] Read the relevant skill(s) **before** coding (per trigger table).
- [ ] Updated matching `SKILL.md` + `reference.md` if behavior or files changed.
- [ ] `AGENTS.md` / `studyverce-overview.mdc` updated if user-visible or cross-cutting.
- [ ] Scoped `.mdc` rule updated when globs cover edited files.
- [ ] **Middleware:** if `apps/web/src/middleware.ts` changed, `config.matcher` is a **static string array** (not imported/spread).
- [ ] **Middleware:** matcher paths still align with `isProtectedAppPath()` in `lib/auth/middleware-routes.ts`.
- [ ] **Redis:** hot paths avoid redundant EVAL/TTL; `/presence` not rate-limited; batch reads use `MGET` where applicable.
- [ ] No documented steps contradict current code.

See `.cursor/skills/README.md` for the skill index.
